# Continue the phased prune from -v2-d.bin, in decreasing order of how much
# anyone would miss what goes.
#
#   nohup ./build-release/bin/zelph < dev_scripts/prune-full-dump-phased-2.zph > run2.log 2>&1 &
#
# Phases A-D (dev_scripts/prune-full-dump-phased.zph) removed 174.7 M of
# 983.4 M nodes and left 73 GB / 178 GiB. That is an order of magnitude above
# the 9 June artifact (6.0 GB / 15.2 GiB), and logs/wikidata-20260309-all.log
# says why: that run used `.prune-nodes A <P> B`, which deletes every SUBJECT
# of a predicate -- P131 13.7 M nodes, P17 5.2 M, P1433 1.1 M, P921 0.6 M --
# where the current script uses .prune-facts, which deletes only the facts and
# leaves the nodes standing. It also pruned scholarly articles and humans.
# Both of those are undone here, in that order.
#
# THE SIZE OF EACH JOB IS PRINTED BEFORE IT STARTS ("Pruning N node(s)"), so
# this script IS the measurement of the four new lines; no separate read-only
# run is needed. Every phase ends in a save, so any of them is a stopping
# point and an artifact.
#
# .cleanup is NOT run per phase. It is a full pass over every node, and this
# engine already removes a pruned node's names with the node, so what it still
# finds is isolated relation nodes -- worth having in a published file, not
# worth paying for five times. dev_scripts/cleanup-artifact.zph does it once,
# on whichever files are chosen for Hugging Face.
#
# The P279 acceptance query runs at the end, as before. On -v2-d it answered
# 141 classes in 18 s; on the 9 June artifact it answers 78. Fewer results
# after these phases is EXPECTED -- pruning instances removes culprits -- but
# an empty answer or an error is not.

.lang wikidata
.load /home/stefan/zelph/wikidata-20260309-all-pruned-v2-d.bin
.stat

# === PHASE E: publications, reached through their properties ===
# `.prune-nodes A (A P B)` deletes every SUBJECT of a predicate. That is the
# shape the 9 June artifact owed its size to and that the current script had
# replaced with .prune-facts, which keeps the nodes. P1433 (published in) and
# P921 (main subject) are carried by publications and by little else.

.prune-nodes A (A P1433 B)
.prune-nodes A (A P921 B)

.stat
.save /home/stefan/zelph/wikidata-20260309-all-pruned-v2-e.bin
.new
.lang wikidata
.load /home/stefan/zelph/wikidata-20260309-all-pruned-v2-e.bin
.stat

# === PHASE F: the rest of academic publishing ===
# P2860 (cites work) is 312.8 M facts, both ends inside this class -- roughly 7
# of the ~16 facts an article carries. .prune-facts costs no cascade, so it
# goes FIRST and takes that weight off every node the next line then walks.

.prune-facts A P2860 B
.prune-nodes A P31 Q13442814
.prune-nodes A P31 Q13433827
.prune-nodes A P31 Q6451276
.prune-nodes A P31 Q23927052
.prune-nodes A P31 Q1143604

.stat
.save /home/stefan/zelph/wikidata-20260309-all-pruned-v2-f.bin
.new
.lang wikidata
.load /home/stefan/zelph/wikidata-20260309-all-pruned-v2-f.bin
.stat

# === PHASE G: everything filed under an administrative entity ===
# Places, buildings, schools, businesses with an address. This is where it
# starts to hurt: the CLASSES stay, the individual items go. 13.7 M nodes in
# the 9 June run, and it ran there after far more had already gone.

.prune-nodes A (A P131 B)

.stat
.save /home/stefan/zelph/wikidata-20260309-all-pruned-v2-g.bin
.new
.lang wikidata
.load /home/stefan/zelph/wikidata-20260309-all-pruned-v2-g.bin
.stat

# === PHASE H: everything with a country ===
# The bluntest line in the file, and deliberately the last but one: almost
# every geographic and organisational item carries P17.

.prune-nodes A (A P17 B)

.stat
.save /home/stefan/zelph/wikidata-20260309-all-pruned-v2-h.bin
.new
.lang wikidata
.load /home/stefan/zelph/wikidata-20260309-all-pruned-v2-h.bin
.stat

# === PHASE I: humans ===
# Last, because for most questions people ask of Wikidata this is the most
# useful class in it. Whether to run this phase at all is a decision, not a
# step -- the artifact saved before it is a legitimate stopping point.

.prune-nodes A P31 Q5
.prune-nodes A P31 Q101352
.prune-nodes A P31 Q12308941
.prune-nodes A P31 Q11879590
.prune-nodes A P31 Q202444
.prune-nodes A P31 Q66480858
.prune-nodes A P31 Q18972207
.prune-nodes A P31 Q79007
.prune-nodes A P31 Q13100073
.prune-nodes A P31 Q4022
.prune-nodes A P31 Q8502
.prune-nodes A P31 Q486972

.stat
.save /home/stefan/zelph/wikidata-20260309-all-pruned-v2-i.bin
.new
.lang wikidata
.load /home/stefan/zelph/wikidata-20260309-all-pruned-v2-i.bin
.stat

# === ACCEPTANCE ===
.import sparql
sparql
PREFIX wd: <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/>
PREFIX wdt: <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/>
SELECT DISTINCT ?class WHERE {
  ?class wdt:P279+ wd:Q215627 .
  ?class wdt:P279+ wd:Q43229 .
  MINUS {
    ?class wdt:P279 ?parent .
    ?parent wdt:P279+ wd:Q215627 .
    ?parent wdt:P279+ wd:Q43229 .
  }
}

.quit
